00:08:55.772 --> 00:08:58.709
I was very uncomfortable with integrity.

00:08:58.709 --> 00:08:59.836
I was uncomfortable sharing

00:08:59.836 --> 00:09:01.630
stories around it because

00:09:01.630 --> 00:09:02.757
it just didn't feel right

00:09:02.757 --> 00:09:04.424
like I did not know,

00:09:05.647 --> 00:09:07.043
like I did not know how

00:09:07.043 --> 00:09:09.126
to articulate my other word,

00:09:09.126 --> 00:09:10.128
but I just knew integrity

00:09:10.128 --> 00:09:11.148
was not right for me.

00:09:11.148 --> 00:09:11.981
We had a meeting.

00:09:11.981 --> 00:09:13.231
- What was the meeting?

00:09:13.231 --> 00:09:14.064
What was the meeting?

00:09:14.064 --> 00:09:14.897
- [Lily] Because I was concerned

00:09:14.897 --> 00:09:15.857
about my one word,

00:09:15.857 --> 00:09:17.032
so I had a meeting with you.

00:09:17.032 --> 00:09:20.115
- Okay, I don't remember that at all.

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:22.855
Okay, and then what happened

00:09:22.855 --> 00:09:24.268
after that meeting?

00:09:24.268 --> 00:09:25.924
- Then we kind of worked through it,

00:09:25.924 --> 00:09:27.899
and then I went to bed that day,

00:09:27.899 --> 00:09:29.233
went to bed that night,

00:09:29.233 --> 00:09:31.141
and then I woke up and then I realized

00:09:31.141 --> 00:09:32.409
I stood for extraordinary because

00:09:32.409 --> 00:09:33.303
I started thinking about

00:09:33.303 --> 00:09:34.328
all the daydreams that

00:09:34.328 --> 00:09:35.880
I used to have as a little girl.

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:37.648
- Somewhere along the way Lily told me

00:09:37.648 --> 00:09:39.480
that she wanted to be a speaker.

00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:41.299
That was your dream to be a speaker.

00:09:41.299 --> 00:09:42.526
You saw yourself on stage.

00:09:42.526 --> 00:09:44.116
You didn't know what your message was.

00:09:44.116 --> 00:09:45.232
- Oh, yes, I remember.

00:09:45.232 --> 00:09:46.296
I don't remember when it was,

00:09:46.296 --> 00:09:47.526
but I remember this conversation,

00:09:47.526 --> 00:09:50.135
and then you said these words,

00:09:50.135 --> 00:09:51.563
which was really interesting,

00:09:51.563 --> 00:09:52.782
it was good, you said,

00:09:52.782 --> 00:09:54.857
"Don't tell me what your vision is

00:09:54.857 --> 00:09:57.049
"because it might just come true."

00:09:57.049 --> 00:09:57.882
- That's true.

00:09:57.882 --> 00:09:58.715
- That's good.

00:09:58.715 --> 00:09:59.548
- Yeah.

00:09:59.548 --> 00:10:00.381
Do you remember what your

00:10:00.381 --> 00:10:01.214
first expresar was?

00:10:01.214 --> 00:10:03.964
- Yes, well, I did a few of them.

00:10:05.003 --> 00:10:06.334
I think the first was

00:10:06.334 --> 00:10:07.253
how to love yourself.

00:10:07.253 --> 00:10:09.143
- So I mean I have a YouTube channel.

00:10:09.143 --> 00:10:10.324
There's an opportunity

00:10:10.324 --> 00:10:11.706
somebody wants to be a speaker

00:10:11.706 --> 00:10:13.502
let's do it come on board be a guest.

00:10:13.502 --> 00:10:15.478
I've on occasion had guests come on,

00:10:15.478 --> 00:10:16.936
and be a part of the videos.

00:10:16.936 --> 00:10:18.550
Alex has been on a number of times

00:10:18.550 --> 00:10:20.597
more about him being a thought leader,

00:10:20.597 --> 00:10:22.868
and getting his skills up there,

00:10:22.868 --> 00:10:24.469
but he doesn't have

00:10:24.469 --> 00:10:26.874
ambitions to be a speaker.

00:10:26.874 --> 00:10:28.234
So, yeah, you told me your goal,

00:10:28.234 --> 00:10:30.149
and we started to make it happen.

00:10:30.149 --> 00:10:32.942
Why did you want to slash my car tires?

00:10:32.942 --> 00:10:34.068
Like there was somewhere there.

00:10:34.068 --> 00:10:34.901
- I'm not violent.

00:10:34.901 --> 00:10:35.734
- No, you totally said,

00:10:35.734 --> 00:10:36.898
you sent me a note

00:10:36.898 --> 00:10:38.732
about slashing my Vespa tires.

00:10:38.732 --> 00:10:39.599
- That was a joke.

00:10:39.599 --> 00:10:41.090
- I gave her the exercise of writing

00:10:41.090 --> 00:10:42.387
her credo and her bio,

00:10:42.387 --> 00:10:43.999
so once you find your one word

00:10:43.999 --> 00:10:45.728
you find your credo you create your bio

00:10:45.728 --> 00:10:47.937
it helps kind of set your path,

00:10:47.937 --> 00:10:49.170
and then she wrote it

00:10:49.170 --> 00:10:50.719
somewhere in the bio she wrote

00:10:50.719 --> 00:10:53.333
"I'm going to slash Evan's Vespa tires"

00:10:53.333 --> 00:10:54.799
as a test to see if

00:10:54.799 --> 00:10:56.966
I actually read it or not.

00:10:58.264 --> 00:11:00.016
I do my work.

00:11:00.016 --> 00:11:00.964
I read it.

00:11:00.964 --> 00:11:01.843
- You read it, see.

00:11:01.843 --> 00:11:02.676
- I read it.

00:11:02.676 --> 00:11:03.969
- You knew it, it was a test.

00:11:03.969 --> 00:11:05.438
- So I was looking for ways to

00:11:05.438 --> 00:11:07.054
again help Lily on her path

00:11:07.054 --> 00:11:07.961
to be a speaker,

00:11:07.961 --> 00:11:09.512
so the YouTube videos was a start.

00:11:09.512 --> 00:11:10.345
- Yes.

00:11:10.345 --> 00:11:11.418
- Then Lily, you know, said,

00:11:11.418 --> 00:11:13.197
"Okay, how about we run a workshop?"

00:11:13.197 --> 00:11:15.220
It's not what we're kind of known for.

00:11:15.220 --> 00:11:16.839
We don't do personal development

00:11:16.839 --> 00:11:19.003
workshops, but we have a studio space.

00:11:19.003 --> 00:11:20.344
We have students.

00:11:20.344 --> 00:11:22.581
Even if only a couple of people show up

00:11:22.581 --> 00:11:25.064
how about we do a workshop

00:11:25.064 --> 00:11:26.459
talking about extraordinary,

00:11:26.459 --> 00:11:27.860
create an extraordinary life,

00:11:27.860 --> 00:11:29.147
and you came in and did that,

00:11:29.147 --> 00:11:30.288
and we met a couple times

00:11:30.288 --> 00:11:32.562
to go over the content.

00:11:32.562 --> 00:11:33.806
I remember the first

00:11:33.806 --> 00:11:36.105
session we had downstairs at Loblaws

00:11:36.105 --> 00:11:38.042
going over the feedback.

00:11:38.042 --> 00:11:38.959
- Oh, yeah.

00:11:38.959 --> 00:11:40.535
- It kind of totally changed

00:11:40.535 --> 00:11:41.593
the direction of.

00:11:41.593 --> 00:11:44.031
- Yeah, because to that point I only

00:11:44.031 --> 00:11:46.031
tested it on my husband,

00:11:47.069 --> 00:11:48.741
and it worked.

00:11:48.741 --> 00:11:50.408
Then when I gave you

00:11:51.571 --> 00:11:53.602
the workshop it didn't make sense,

00:11:53.602 --> 00:11:54.767
so I end up going back,

00:11:54.767 --> 00:11:56.718
and scrapping everything,

00:11:56.718 --> 00:11:58.775
which took me 100 hours

00:11:58.775 --> 00:12:00.930
to make to begin with,

00:12:00.930 --> 00:12:02.849
and then I went back and that week

00:12:02.849 --> 00:12:04.771
I completely changed it,

00:12:04.771 --> 00:12:08.269
and then I delivered it a week later.

00:12:08.269 --> 00:12:09.639
- So we met like a week before

00:12:09.639 --> 00:12:11.360
to go over the content,

00:12:11.360 --> 00:12:14.138
and answer questions and ease nerves.

00:12:14.138 --> 00:12:15.524
I think the biggest challenge was

00:12:15.524 --> 00:12:17.644
you created a workshop around

00:12:17.644 --> 00:12:18.858
an extraordinary life

00:12:18.858 --> 00:12:20.224
for what extraordinary means to you.

00:12:20.224 --> 00:12:21.057
- Exactly.

00:12:21.057 --> 00:12:22.059
- But not allowing ...

00:12:22.059 --> 00:12:23.274
- Not use their values of my own values.

00:12:23.274 --> 00:12:24.873
- Right, we want to allow them

00:12:24.873 --> 00:12:26.216
to define what it means for them

00:12:26.216 --> 00:12:27.509
that was the difference.

00:12:27.509 --> 00:12:28.628
I think that was the biggest difference.

00:12:28.628 --> 00:12:30.712
I mean we ran the workshop,

00:12:30.712 --> 00:12:32.862
and it was good.

00:12:32.862 --> 00:12:34.406
How many people?

00:12:34.406 --> 00:12:36.183
10 people showed up for the first one.

00:12:36.183 --> 00:12:37.119
Something like that.

00:12:37.119 --> 00:12:37.952
- It was good.

00:12:37.952 --> 00:12:40.080
- People enjoyed it, good feedback,

00:12:40.080 --> 00:12:41.786
and then from there we talked about

00:12:41.786 --> 00:12:44.659
having potential one word workshops,

00:12:44.659 --> 00:12:46.180
said, hey, people are

00:12:46.180 --> 00:12:47.091
asking to do workshops,

00:12:47.091 --> 00:12:49.201
I don't want to really do workshops,

00:12:49.201 --> 00:12:50.370
but there's an opportunity

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:51.557
maybe you could do it.

00:12:51.557 --> 00:12:53.271
We were also thinking about implementing

00:12:53.271 --> 00:12:56.316
it more within TDS culture at the time,

00:12:56.316 --> 00:12:57.954
so having Lily do regular

00:12:57.954 --> 00:12:59.466
workshops from the studio.

00:12:59.466 --> 00:13:01.049
We had a discussion remember before

00:13:01.049 --> 00:13:01.882
saying like listen,

00:13:01.882 --> 00:13:02.811
this has to be something that

00:13:02.811 --> 00:13:04.609
you fully believe in and understand.

00:13:04.609 --> 00:13:07.381
I get it, it's my message.

00:13:07.381 --> 00:13:09.716
It has to be your message, too.

00:13:09.716 --> 00:13:10.927
It's okay to have your own spin on it,

00:13:10.927 --> 00:13:12.539
and your own take on it, you know,

00:13:12.539 --> 00:13:13.720
Lily delivers it in a way

00:13:13.720 --> 00:13:15.051
that's slightly different

00:13:15.051 --> 00:13:15.970
than what I would do,

00:13:15.970 --> 00:13:16.835
but you have to believe in

00:13:16.835 --> 00:13:18.017
what's in the book,

00:13:18.017 --> 00:13:20.693
and not be teaching something that

00:13:20.693 --> 00:13:22.711
you don't wholeheartedly believe in.

00:13:22.711 --> 00:13:23.544
Then you took it a couple of days.

00:13:23.544 --> 00:13:24.377
- Yeah.

00:13:24.377 --> 00:13:25.210
- I don't know if you read

00:13:25.210 --> 00:13:26.043
the book again or you're listening

00:13:26.043 --> 00:13:26.876
to the audio version or?

00:13:26.876 --> 00:13:28.235
- I read the first portion of it.

00:13:28.235 --> 00:13:29.464
Well, I read the book

00:13:29.464 --> 00:13:31.489
a couple of times to that point.

00:13:31.489 --> 00:13:33.536
I was actually really proud of myself

00:13:33.536 --> 00:13:35.021
that I took a couple of days.

00:13:35.021 --> 00:13:36.621
- Wait, wasn't it the first book that

00:13:36.621 --> 00:13:37.572
you've read in like

00:13:37.572 --> 00:13:39.035
20 years or something?

00:13:39.035 --> 00:13:40.785
- 20, yes, it's true.

00:13:42.033 --> 00:13:42.866
I was really proud of myself

00:13:42.866 --> 00:13:45.095
for doing that because

00:13:45.095 --> 00:13:46.495
originally I would have

00:13:46.495 --> 00:13:48.544
just said yes at that moment.

00:13:48.544 --> 00:13:50.323
I was almost sure, I was almost sure

00:13:50.323 --> 00:13:51.714
that I was going to do it,

00:13:51.714 --> 00:13:53.856
but I really wanted to make sure that

00:13:53.856 --> 00:13:55.507
if it's a mission that

00:13:55.507 --> 00:13:57.154
I want to be part of

00:13:57.154 --> 00:13:58.834
I wanted to see that.

00:13:58.834 --> 00:14:02.691
I took a few days and I realized that

00:14:02.691 --> 00:14:04.642
we're very similar.

00:14:04.642 --> 00:14:06.019
It's very important to know

00:14:06.019 --> 00:14:06.852
what you stand for

00:14:06.852 --> 00:14:08.713
in order to go out there, do things,

00:14:08.713 --> 00:14:09.736
so I jumped on the mission,

00:14:09.736 --> 00:14:11.762
and then I did the workshops.

00:14:11.762 --> 00:14:14.179
After the workshop I sent you

00:14:15.278 --> 00:14:16.959
a Facebook message saying

00:14:16.959 --> 00:14:19.308
thank you for giving me the opportunity,

00:14:19.308 --> 00:14:21.202
and then you wrote back and said,

00:14:21.202 --> 00:14:22.935
"I have an idea for you."

00:14:22.935 --> 00:14:24.811
Then I got so excited I actually

00:14:24.811 --> 00:14:26.112
had a meeting that night.

00:14:26.112 --> 00:14:26.956
- Okay.

00:14:26.956 --> 00:14:28.917
- That I kind of put off because

00:14:28.917 --> 00:14:30.550
I knew something great was stewing.

00:14:30.550 --> 00:14:31.387
- All right.

00:14:31.387 --> 00:14:32.471
- I knew there was something.

00:14:32.471 --> 00:14:33.468
I just had a feeling.

00:14:33.468 --> 00:14:35.107
- I like telling people I have

00:14:35.107 --> 00:14:36.108
an idea for them,

00:14:36.108 --> 00:14:37.778
and then let them sit on that

00:14:37.778 --> 00:14:39.415
for a day or two and then I show up.

00:14:39.415 --> 00:14:40.248
- No, I can't wait

00:14:40.248 --> 00:14:41.577
a day or two, no, never.

00:14:41.577 --> 00:14:44.083
- Curiosity is part of the process.

00:14:44.083 --> 00:14:44.916
- Never.

00:14:44.916 --> 00:14:46.033
- So I think I was just impressed

00:14:46.033 --> 00:14:47.068
with the workshop.

00:14:47.068 --> 00:14:47.901
I was at the workshop.

00:14:47.901 --> 00:14:49.450
I didn't say anything.

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:50.770
People got a free copy of the book,

00:14:50.770 --> 00:14:52.163
and I signed autographs,

00:14:52.163 --> 00:14:53.415
and answered questions at the end,

00:14:53.415 --> 00:14:54.790
but throughout the workshop

00:14:54.790 --> 00:14:56.704
Lily handled everything.

00:14:56.704 --> 00:14:58.867
It's intimidating, too, first like

00:14:58.867 --> 00:15:00.418
that was a bigger ...

00:15:00.418 --> 00:15:01.374
- Was it 30 somewhat people?

00:15:01.374 --> 00:15:02.422
- 30 something people.

00:15:02.422 --> 00:15:04.162
I'm there, too, right?

00:15:04.162 --> 00:15:05.736
So like 30 something people.

00:15:05.736 --> 00:15:06.724
I'm there, you know,

00:15:06.724 --> 00:15:07.801
the author of the book

00:15:07.801 --> 00:15:09.359
I can imagine it's intimidating

00:15:09.359 --> 00:15:10.533
to be sitting there presenting

00:15:10.533 --> 00:15:13.322
somebody else's material.

00:15:13.322 --> 00:15:14.155
Then there were some tough questions, too,

00:15:14.155 --> 00:15:17.155
which you did a great job answering.

00:15:22.573 --> 00:15:24.815
She could have easily deferred it to me.

00:15:24.815 --> 00:15:28.000
It's like, well, Evan, what do you think?

00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:29.406
She just chose to answer,

00:15:29.406 --> 00:15:30.316
which was great.

00:15:30.316 --> 00:15:31.149
- Never.

00:15:31.149 --> 00:15:31.982
- That impressed me.

00:15:31.982 --> 00:15:32.815
One great thing about Lily

00:15:32.815 --> 00:15:34.300
if it's going to make her

00:15:34.300 --> 00:15:35.133
feel uncomfortable

00:15:35.133 --> 00:15:36.374
then she wants to go out and do it.

00:15:36.374 --> 00:15:38.040
It's like jump into

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:39.011
that made me feel really uncomfortable,

00:15:39.011 --> 00:15:40.582
so I have to go out and do it.

00:15:40.582 --> 00:15:41.696
It's like the default mindset,

00:15:41.696 --> 00:15:42.626
which is good.

00:15:42.626 --> 00:15:44.793
We met and I had this idea

00:15:49.036 --> 00:15:51.713
to try to turn Lily into a speaker,

00:15:51.713 --> 00:15:53.327
and make it a business,

00:15:53.327 --> 00:15:54.476
and leaver her job.

00:15:54.476 --> 00:15:56.832
You had changed your job

00:15:56.832 --> 00:15:58.402
like a year ago same company,

00:15:58.402 --> 00:15:59.302
but you kind of ...

00:15:59.302 --> 00:16:00.135
- A couple of years ago.

00:16:00.135 --> 00:16:00.968
- Something like that.

00:16:00.968 --> 00:16:02.350
- I moved around and I was actually

00:16:02.350 --> 00:16:04.901
when you approached me I was at a job

00:16:04.901 --> 00:16:06.663
that I was pretty content with.

00:16:06.663 --> 00:16:08.965
I was content and I didn't hate it

00:16:08.965 --> 00:16:10.577
like I actually liked it,

00:16:10.577 --> 00:16:12.894
so that's when you approached me.

00:16:12.894 --> 00:16:14.302
- Yeah, so the idea is

00:16:14.302 --> 00:16:17.207
to turn it into a business.

00:16:17.207 --> 00:16:18.894
Turn Lily, modest speaker,

00:16:18.894 --> 00:16:20.033
into a business.

00:16:20.033 --> 00:16:22.022
It was one of those heart decisions

00:16:22.022 --> 00:16:24.533
for me because at the time I mean

00:16:24.533 --> 00:16:25.919
I had my YouTube channel,

00:16:25.919 --> 00:16:26.920
I had my main business

00:16:26.920 --> 00:16:28.269
it takes up a ton of my time.

00:16:28.269 --> 00:16:29.908
I have TDS which was still growing,

00:16:29.908 --> 00:16:31.615
and still lots to do,

00:16:31.615 --> 00:16:33.288
and still more mentorship for Alex

00:16:33.288 --> 00:16:34.387
before we get to the point

00:16:34.387 --> 00:16:35.326
where we need to be.

00:16:35.326 --> 00:16:36.865
It's like time is crunched.

00:16:36.865 --> 00:16:39.919
Don't have the time for this,

00:16:39.919 --> 00:16:41.790
but this is the timing.

00:16:41.790 --> 00:16:43.117
It feels right I'm going to go.

00:16:43.117 --> 00:16:44.490
I actually didn't think you were

00:16:44.490 --> 00:16:45.516
going to say yes, surprisingly enough.

00:16:45.516 --> 00:16:46.349
- Really?

00:16:46.349 --> 00:16:50.344
- I would have put it at like 35%.

00:16:50.344 --> 00:16:51.177
- Really?

00:16:51.177 --> 00:16:53.412
- Yeah, I would have said 35%,

00:16:53.412 --> 00:16:56.204
but at least not yet not on the spot

00:16:56.204 --> 00:16:57.728
like, maybe, okay, let me think about,

00:16:57.728 --> 00:16:59.859
you know, maybe in the next six months,

00:16:59.859 --> 00:17:00.982
a year, or something,

00:17:00.982 --> 00:17:02.897
so that was what I was expecting

00:17:02.897 --> 00:17:03.899
kind of going in,

00:17:03.899 --> 00:17:05.005
but you know I'll put it on the radar,

00:17:05.005 --> 00:17:06.700
and I'll see what happens,

00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:08.324
but then I said to her, you know,

00:17:08.324 --> 00:17:09.157
if she says yes,

00:17:09.157 --> 00:17:11.657
and if it's great let's do it.

00:17:13.355 --> 00:17:14.298
There was no regret, or anything there,

00:17:14.298 --> 00:17:16.260
but, yeah, I was a little off

00:17:16.260 --> 00:17:18.304
in the percentage, so.

00:17:18.304 --> 00:17:19.191
- Interesting.

00:17:19.191 --> 00:17:20.024
- Yeah, that was good.

00:17:20.024 --> 00:17:20.857
- I was 100% sure.

00:17:20.857 --> 00:17:22.602
Now looking back in retrospect

00:17:22.602 --> 00:17:23.991
it was probably like one of

00:17:23.991 --> 00:17:26.106
the easiest decisions I had to make,

00:17:26.106 --> 00:17:28.391
and the rest I would have figured out

